00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
if you are new here my name is elizabeth  i'm a medical student and an artist  living  in london and today i wanted to answer  one of the questions  i get asked the most which is just how i  manage my time and how i don't  procrastinate  now this is a very loaded question  because the thing is  i do procrastinate a lot and i  absolutely  love it i don't know anyone who doesn't  and i don't actually think that  procrastination itself is the issue  so i spent some time thinking about it  and in this video  i'm going to share how i get so much  done  while also procrastinating and what sort  of schedule changes and  mind shift changes have completely  transformed the way i work  and my results obviously this will just  be what has worked for me  and i can only hope that if you do watch  this video you can also find it valuable  starting from the beginning  i have always been a massive fan of  scheduling  massive i would be given any sort of  projects and i would  turn into the most inspired scheduling  queen i have tried everything making  calendars to span  a whole wall redoing my notion google  calendar  apple calendars bullet journaling you  name it the thing is that this  over-excitable over-inspired version of  elizabeth  although she's very good at scheduling  she doesn't exist  all the time the version of myself that  actually  shows up three days later to do the work  is  quite lazy bored would rather just lie  on the bed and do  nothing or she'll find her instagram  feed to be the most  interesting thing in the world and  therefore the work  won't always get done so what would  happen is that very soon i would start  falling behind  and once these little slip-ups  accumulate because i had  such a strict schedule in days weeks  or in the best case scenario months that  schedule would be  completely pointless there would be not  a chance that i would be able to catch  up with it so there would just be  useless plans that i would have to  throw away and on top of that because i  now  had such bad feelings associated with  the job that i wanted to do i would end  up quitting a lot of things  this could be a new workout plan or a  new project or studying a new language  or learning a new skill  i would just stop now i've changed the  way that i approach things even before i  get started  and what i mean by this is that i never  forget that i  am a huge procrastinator some of my most  relaxing and enjoyable times  are when i'm procrastinating for example  when i sit by my windowsill and look out  into the city  listening to music and doing absolutely  nothing this  is so much fun for me and the point of  my life is not just to get things done  because the point of those things in  themselves is to make my life better  and sometimes my life is made better by  simply doing  nothing so now when i schedule things  which i still  very very much enjoy doing i do it in a  way that allows me to feel  just as good when i'm working and  getting things done  as when i'm doing absolutely nothing so  practically what this means for me is  that most projects i will do in a single  day  and in the single sitting i will take  advantage of those times where i'm  hyper-inspired i'm very much the sort of  person who can work  for almost 20 hours in a row sometimes  and i'll get most  major projects done in those bouts of  inspiration  but usually it's not these that are the  issue  the issue is with the things that we  have to do consistently  over a long period of time and this is  where  my scheduling comes in i create very lax  schedules i almost never plan to do the  same thing  two days in a row and i space things out  a lot  i'm very generous with myself in this  way there are days where i'll literally  be up until 6am  doing not only what i have planned for  that day on the projects  but what i've planned for the whole next  two weeks because i'm super inspired  and then there'll be times where i just  won't touch something for weeks or even  months because i'm just not  in the mood for it even though in the  past i would have thought that in those  times  i've quit the thing is i haven't because  my planning  is so relaxed i'm always catching up  with myself one way or another  and i'm always up to date honestly so  for example you might see me  not working out throughout the whole  third lockdown or  equally not drawing or painting  throughout the whole third lockdown  this doesn't mean that i'm not an artist  or very much into fitness i just don't  see things that way  anymore i plan for the very long term  and i know that for both of these things  i haven't quit because i have made up  for it in the past by doing extra work  and i know that this is something that i  will do again in the future i am always  working consistently  just on a larger time scale if you were  to zoom out and look at my life  in terms of months or years i would be  working consistently and still doing  things  compared to what i was doing before  where i'd be hyper consistent on the  daily level for a very short period of  time  and then just stop all together and the  issue for me has always been consistency  if i am being consistent i am winning  i'm doing things right  so honestly how i get things done is i  just follow my fun  and what i feel like doing in the moment  it works and it works really well  if you're a student and you are curious  on how i actually plan my study  schedules  i have a video when i go through that in  a lot more detail and if you're someone  who wants to take up a new project or  hobby  using the same schedule would be very  very effective hopefully because that's  the same thing that i do as always thank  you for spending this time with me i  hope you found  anything that came out of my face today  useful i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day  be kind yourself and others and don't  believe everything you think thanks  bye  [Music]

